WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.839
This is where we left off in the previous video.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.380
We mounted plant cells and animal cells on

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.599
slides to observe them under the microscope.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.480
Let us study them in general in this video.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.400
For our convenience let us select just one…say

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.290
the onion peel cells to understand the structure

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.380
and the contents of the cells.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.160
Roughly, we have these thick, distinct borders

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.000
that differentiate each cell from the other

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.369
one!

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:35.950
Then we have these tiny dark spots scattered all over!

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.940
Also, we can spot this prominent, circular

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.460
structure here which is very darkly stained.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.350
Any idea what these things are?

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:47.320
Well, these are the cell constituents.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:51.180
Let us get introduced to each.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:54.960
This outer margin seen here is called the CELL WALL.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.356
If we zoom in a bit, we notice that there

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:59.810
is another layer on the inner side of this

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:01.190
cell wall.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:03.130
This is called the cell MEMBRANE.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:06.026
Yes, the outer wall is the cell wall and the

00:01:06.026 --> 00:01:08.659
inner layer is called the cell MEMBRANE.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.100
The cell membrane is also referred to as the

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.799
PLASMA membrane.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.380
It is POROUS in nature.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.500
Hold on… what does ‘porous’ mean?

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.897
It simply means that “any material can move

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.840
in and out of the plasma membrane”.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.980
But isn’t that dangerous?

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.049
Of course it is!

00:01:27.049 --> 00:01:29.440
But the simple solution lies in the nature

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:30.920
of the plasma membrane.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.420
That is because it is ‘SELECTIVELY PERMEABLE’.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.759
Now what does selectively permeable mean here?

00:01:38.759 --> 00:01:41.224
Just like a guard standing at the office door

00:01:41.224 --> 00:01:43.579
who allows only members with identity cards

00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:47.198
to enter and exit, the plasma membrane also

00:01:47.198 --> 00:01:51.069
allows only SPECIFIC materials to move across.

00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:55.409
We will look at this in details in our upcoming video.

00:01:55.409 --> 00:01:57.410
This was just to understand how the plasma

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.160
membrane is selectively permeable!

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:03.679
Now let us move ahead to know about the cell wall.

00:02:03.679 --> 00:02:06.289
Do you think ALL cells have cell walls?

00:02:06.289 --> 00:02:08.039
Well the answer is a no!

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:11.680
That is because animal cells do NOT have cell walls.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:15.391
An animal cell only has the plasma membrane

00:02:15.391 --> 00:02:17.290
and not the cell wall.

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:21.150
The ‘cell walls’ act as PROTECTORS for plant cells.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:24.080
It is composed of a NON-LIVING rigid structure

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.760
that is CELLULOSE.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.080
It not only acts as a protector but also gives

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.360
a proper SHAPE to the plant cells.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:35.420
It also helps in cell-to-cell interactions

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:39.100
and provides a barrier to undesirable macromolecules.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.437
It protects, it gives shape to the cells,

00:02:43.437 --> 00:02:46.610
and it helps in cell to cell interactions!

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:49.140
Clearly, the cell wall is a VERY important

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.140
part of the plant cell structure.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:55.480
Now let’s get into this lighter region here.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.840
This lighter region is the CYTOPLASM.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:03.019
It is a jelly like substance filling up the cell space.

00:03:03.019 --> 00:03:07.190
And these tiny parts in the cytoplasm are the organelles.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:09.230
And what exactly are they?

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:12.220
Just like the human body has different organs,

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:14.760
the cell has various organelles.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.553
And just like the organs, each organelle performs

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:18.840
a different function.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.300
Let us study each organelle and its functions

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.780
in our upcoming videos!

